# A simple demonstration based on Table 4.2 in Design Engineering and Science by Suh, Cavique, and Foley (2021)

DEFINE FR1 as Brake vehicle
DEFINE DP1 as Brake system
COUPLE FR1 to DP1 because Most simple implementation
DEFINE FR1.1 as Brake power density
DEFINE DP1.1 as Disk brakes
COUPLE FR1.1 to DP1.1 because Efficiently dissipate energy
DEFINE FR1.1.1 as Dissipate heat
DEFINE DP1.1.1 as Self-cooling disks
COUPLE FR1.1.1 to DP1.1.1 because Cooling with no extra parts
DEFINE FR1.1.1.1 as Maintain surface contact
DEFINE DP1.1.1.1 as Determine roughness
COUPLE FR1.1.1.1 to DP1.1.1.1 because Aids in control of surface contact
DEFINE CN1 as Control vehicle speed
COUPLE CN1 to FR1 because Deceleration is half the battle
DEFINE PV1 as Fabricate braking subassembly
DEFINE PV1.1 as Machine brake disks
DEFINE PV1.1.1 as Welded cooling fins in disk
DEFINE PV1.1.1.1 as Use roughness gauge
ACCEPT PV1.1.1.1 because Acceptable gauge available
COUPLE DP1.1.1.1 to PV1.1.1.1 because Acceptable method
